      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it may be a mistake.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6400 mg/day.** The usual maximum is 3200 mg/day, and the usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. The 1600 mg dose is double the single-dose maximum, and the daily total is double the daily maximum.\n\nOptions:\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum). This is the top of the labeled range.\n2. **A lower dose**, such as 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours, if you want less NSAID exposure.\n3. **Your original order as written**, if you intended it. I'd still want you to confirm it, since it exceeds standard maximums.\n\nSince this is a 70-year-old on the medicine service, the NSAID risks (GI bleeding, renal effects, fluid retention, cardiovascular risk) are worth weighing. Also check whether the patient is on anticoagulants, antiplatelets, ACE inhibitors, ARBs, or diuretics.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter? Or should I enter the order exactly as you wrote it?"
      }
